      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WORTHY GEM (1) has the strongest exposed profile, with a win at this track two starts ago in 3-4yo Open grade and a forgivable Townsville fourth last start after being bumped early and held up from the 250m. Gets the key booking of Wiggins and looks the one to beat. FORMAL AFFAIR (4) is the main danger after a sound Bowen second and a prior win at this venue, with Kennedy's record on her adding to the case, though her record around 1250m is the query. BOOMING BELIEF (7) keeps racing honestly, placed at her past two and already placed around this distance, but has to convert. BANK INTEREST (6) is still a maiden, yet his last two beaten margins were narrow and he gets weight relief. Not underestimating. RED LIGHT POWER (5) has been flat in her two runs back but now gets the blinkers on first time to hopefully spark her to life. Keeping safe.",
